<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:41:58 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Mass burials held in Nepal as bodies wash up after catastrophic flooding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding</link><description>
Every day, new bodies are recovered in Nepal, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the disaster, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Morgues in the country's main cities are reaching capacity. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification. France 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fca13ff0-a633-11f1-a97d-af91c05e98b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:40:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After the floods, Nepal works to bury hundreds of washed-up unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
Nepal is burying dozens of bodies in multiple trenches as Nepal’s disaster agency said that 1,003 deaths had been counted there, with 3,916 people missing, including 583 foreign nationals. In its latest update, China reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, including 261 foreigners. Crews faced challenging conditions as they searched unstable terrain and piles of debris. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f853d4b2-a606-11f1-aceb-77a48fff9120</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:08:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal's rescuers navigate mud-swamped tunnels for hundreds of missing workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers</link><description>
The death toll in Nepal has crossed 1,000 from the deadly floods that tore through an area on the border with Tibet on August 26, and nearly 4,000 people remain missing. six days on hopes for survivors are dimming, but rescuers focused on a network of hydropower sites along the Trishuli River are holding out hope. Of the roughly 900 workers missing, some 500 people are believed to be trapped in the tunnels, according to Nepalese authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04b62fcc-a605-11f1-863b-f9580e1f490b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:59:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal races to find hundreds stuck in hydropower tunnels following floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods</link><description>
More than 1,000 people have been killed in the devastating floods that struck the border between Nepal and Tibet. Authorities have started mass burials for unclaimed bodies while they wait for victims' families to claim them. Meanwhile, rescue operations are underway to rescue hundreds of workers stuck in hydropower tunnels. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more from the Chitwan district in Nepal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cedbe370-a5ea-11f1-92eb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T070640Z-911836291-RC22ANADUOGL-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cedbe370-a5ea-11f1-92eb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T070640Z-911836291-RC22ANADUOGL-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">073787cc-a5e3-11f1-ae76-37353d2a8c86</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:53:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Tibetan activists accuse China of underreporting flood death toll</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260901-tibetan-activists-accuse-china-of-underreporting-flood-death-toll</link><description>
Tibetan exiles and activists have accused China of severely underreporting the death toll from the devastating Himalayan floods along its border with Nepal. Beijing has reported 16 deaths and 546 missing in Tibet so far and the foreign ministry insists that the release of information has been "open, transparent and timely".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05815cbc-a5db-11f1-a89c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2421b82212fd90daef576b14d5eeb8c747bda2f4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05815cbc-a5db-11f1-a89c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2421b82212fd90daef576b14d5eeb8c747bda2f4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06dda5a2-a5db-11f1-a4b6-599faa1a754c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 07:59:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05815cbc-a5db-11f1-a89c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2421b82212fd90daef576b14d5eeb8c747bda2f4.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA['Glaciers in Himalayas retreating': Nepal floods triggered by 'glacier collapse & massive landslide']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landslide</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Joseph Shea, Glaciologist and Associate Professor at the University of Northern BC. Shea argues that the catastrophe should be understood as a compound event in which a glacier failure and a massive landslide occurred together. His analysis places the disaster within the broader, well-established transformation of the Himalayas under climate change. As warming changes high-mountain environments, scientists may increasingly need to identify subtle precursors to rare but potentially devastating cascading hazards.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a287636c-a5cc-11f1-b610-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-151021-151029-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a287636c-a5cc-11f1-b610-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-151021-151029-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7e7886e-a5cc-11f1-9d7d-71e2923d9923</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 06:26:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Sea change: Much of the world's economic GDP has moved to the Asia-Pacific region'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitter</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Rana Mitter, historian, author and ST Lee Chair in US-Asia Relations at the Harvard Kennedy School. He discusses the significance of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) as it pertains to the evolution of a changing international system, this as the bloc holds a summit in Kyrgyzstan's capital Bishkek.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29d4c974-a5e4-11f1-9a79-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10759445966a9695275f2978-38064414.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29d4c974-a5e4-11f1-9a79-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10759445966a9695275f2978-38064414.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29f2fde6-a5c5-11f1-9153-0376ece26ef1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 05:22:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Melting Himalayas? Nepal disaster exposes growing risk of glacial flooding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding</link><description>
It may well be one of the tragic consequences of global warming. Scientists will tell us whether receding glaciers are to blame for last Wednesday’s ice shelf collapse that triggered a catastrophic flood, cascading down more than 3,000 metres from the Chinese border into Nepal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/249699be-a563-11f1-a85a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T171033Z-78116127-RC2Y8NA7BWYN-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/249699be-a563-11f1-a85a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T171033Z-78116127-RC2Y8NA7BWYN-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd2dd5b4-a55a-11f1-a457-7f5203728eaa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:35:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal-Tibet flood death toll surpasses 1,000</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet</link><description>
Rescuers battled mud and debris Monday as the death toll from devastating glacial floods along the China-Nepal border topped 1,000, with nearly 4,500 people still missing. Rescue teams continued a desperate search for survivors as entire communities were swept away.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45ee7412-a593-11f1-93a6-2d6b79c37be8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:34:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg">© Dar Yasin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Nepal disaster: Fake and AI images flood social media as deaths mount</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount</link><description>
As deadly floods hit the Nepal-China border, social media is being inundated with fake and misleading footage. In Truth or Fake, Vedika Bahl goes through viral videos falsely linked to the disaster, including AI-generated content and old recycled footage from India, Chile and Alaska. Some posts have racked up millions of views online, exploiting the tragedy to drive engagement for easy clicks or further perpetuate conspiracy theories. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e5ae9d8-a570-11f1-9682-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-499210196a95d2ac205d05-65537713.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e5ae9d8-a570-11f1-9682-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-499210196a95d2ac205d05-65537713.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96bbde54-a56e-11f1-ab3b-01902f20a226</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:00:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hundreds feared stuck in hydropower tunnels as flood deaths surpass 950 in Nepal and China</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china</link><description>
Rescuers raced Monday to free hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in tunnels at hydropower sites that were buried in mud by catastrophic flooding on the Nepal-China border, as the death toll climbed and increasingly desperate families searched for missing loved ones. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe94334-a569-11f1-a255-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-200222-200417-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe94334-a569-11f1-a255-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-200222-200417-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1588ae6-a569-11f1-8eca-0d645d89d448</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:34:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f79b8a8-a551-11f1-990a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-130116-130953-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f79b8a8-a551-11f1-990a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-130116-130953-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">555efac6-a551-11f1-8748-494925e89fd0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:52:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canberra's zoo treats its residents to personnalised musical therapy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy</link><description>
A music therapist in Australia has been playing for animals at Canberra's zoo for the last five years. It's a relaxing experience for animals and staff alike and the animals all react differently to the music played.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a79d9c30-a550-11f1-87fe-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9018595896a959dacb778b6-97867539.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a79d9c30-a550-11f1-87fe-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9018595896a959dacb778b6-97867539.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e0b78e2e-a526-11f1-8be7-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:30:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal deadly floods: FRANCE 24 report – on the ground with survivors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-%E2%80%93-on-the-ground-with-survivors</link><description>
In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. While rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur in the Nuwako district – one of the villages hit by the flood on August 26.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb8e6162-a54b-11f1-8af0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mininepal.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb8e6162-a54b-11f1-8af0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mininepal.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33e47862-a54c-11f1-ad65-d7a1b5a4e79c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:12:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal grapples with destruction and loss in wake of deadly floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods</link><description>
Authorities in Nepal have warned of possible fresh flooding after water levels rose in the Bhotekoshi River. The floods took place after a glacier collapse. They have killed at least 900 people - with more than 4,000 others missing in Nepal and Tibet. Now, a massive rescue effort continues and communities grapple with devastation and loss.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ed2d33c-a4de-11f1-abad-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T164052Z-1845982200-RC2Y8NALSAGW-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ed2d33c-a4de-11f1-abad-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T164052Z-1845982200-RC2Y8NALSAGW-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33d4d422-a53b-11f1-9302-7f7d0767bf74</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:10:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal races to find its missing as flood area remains largely inaccessible</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible</link><description>
Nepal's rescuers are racing against the clock to find the over 4,000 people missing after the flash floods that devastated an area in the north of the country on August 26. Rescue operations include one where workers are trying to save hundreds believed to be stuck inside a blocked hydropower project. Meanwhile, authorities have started burying unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f65b05c8-a538-11f1-bfa5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T110221Z-1880862988-RC2L9NASZHK5-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f65b05c8-a538-11f1-bfa5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T110221Z-1880862988-RC2L9NASZHK5-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4b63796-a537-11f1-8ca5-b57e20c7a62b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:41:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After the floods, Nepal's survivors look to rebuilding their lives</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives</link><description>
In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. In the devastated villages, families lost everything in minutes. And while rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur, in the Nuwako district, one of the villages hit by the flood of August 26.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7595c480-a526-11f1-a05e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-103720-103949-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7595c480-a526-11f1-a05e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-103720-103949-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7aaf5a94-a526-11f1-aee9-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:53:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal starts burying its dead as search for over 4,200 missing continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues</link><description>
The combined deaths in Nepal and China surpassed 900, with more than 4,700 people missing. It also includes 933 workers on hydropower projects along the river which the torrent crashed through. With morgues running at full capacity, the country has started to bury unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 244s Shazaib Wahlah tells us more from a grief-stricken Nepal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6613b04c-a519-11f1-857c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T073233Z-1269427110-RC2H9NAF3LO1-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-FAMILIES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6613b04c-a519-11f1-857c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T073233Z-1269427110-RC2H9NAF3LO1-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-FAMILIES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1bd2f60-a522-11f1-a588-41b48f6f83b3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:33:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What to know about the SCO, the summit billed as a counterweight to US influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence</link><description>
The leaders of China, Russia and India are among the heads of state gathering in Kyrgyzstan for the summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization. The summit is celebrating its 25 years in existence. Although the group is billed as a counterweight to US. global influence, it is not the case for all participating countries. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry takes a look at what the SCO is, and what will be discussed this year.
